_model: definition
---
title: Definition 1
---
order: 1
---
short_label: X.Def.II.1
---
statement: Given a rational straight line and a binomial, divided into its terms, such that the square on the greater term is greater than the square on the lesser by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with the greater, then, if the greater term is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, let the whole be called a <i>first binomial</i> straight line;
---
group: defX.II
---
subsection: II
---
body:

